From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OHOS Build <build@ohos>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 01:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skip gengetopt/help2man requirements for cross-build

The upstream configure.ac hard-fails if help2man or gengetopt are
missing.  For cross-compilation to OHOS neither tool is available
in the SDK, so:
  - Remove the AC_MSG_ERROR checks for help2man and gengetopt.
  - Drop the `src' subdirectory from SUBDIRS (it needs gengetopt to
    generate cmdline.c/cmdline.h for the u2f-server CLI utility).

The library (libu2f-server) itself does not depend on these tools.

--- a/Makefile.am	2026-09-04 08:47:59.547248906 +0800
+++ b/Makefile.am	2026-09-04 08:47:59.583247656 +0800
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
 # (INCLUDING NEGLIGENCE OR OTHERWISE) ARISING IN ANY WAY OUT OF THE USE
 # OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.
 
-SUBDIRS = u2f-server src
+SUBDIRS = u2f-server
 
 if ENABLE_TESTS
 SUBDIRS+=tests
--- a/configure.ac	2026-09-04 08:47:59.563248593 +0800
+++ b/configure.ac	2026-09-04 08:47:59.627247968 +0800
@@ -51,12 +51,6 @@
 
 AM_MISSING_PROG(HELP2ADOC, help2adoc, $missing_dir)
 AM_MISSING_PROG(HELP2MAN, help2man, $missing_dir)
-if ! which help2man >/dev/null ; then
-   AC_MSG_ERROR([help2man missing])
-fi
-if ! which gengetopt >/dev/null ; then
-   AC_MSG_ERROR([gengetopt missing])
-fi
 
 gl_LD_VERSION_SCRIPT
 
